 "note": "What the ledger does not know, as SETS of identities. A member may leave; a new member fails CI. Sets rather than counts because a count is defeated by a swap — add one undocumented variant, document a different one, and the total is unchanged while the ledger knows strictly less about a new string. The guard also compares against the MERGE BASE, so raising the file in the same commit as the regression does not help. Raising requires a dated reason under `raised`. ADR-019 D8. Live: observations-status.py --unproven",
 "raised": {
  "manual_reverify": {
   "date": "2026-09-07",
   "members": [
    "2026-09-07-the-qualification-table-is-a-one-language-table"
   ],
   "reason": "The record measures a test whose outcome depends on Logic's UI LANGUAGE, and the language only takes on a fresh process. So reverifying means quitting Logic, which raises a save sheet, relaunching on the fixture, and doing it twice. A script can do all of that — `locale-campaign.sh` does — but that script also censuses and files records, and pointing a reverify at it would make re-checking this claim write six new files. The honest form is a person following the four commands the record lists."
  },
