   "reason": "The same shape as the five Japanese forms raised 2026-09-07, and for the same reason. All five German strings were READ — off the 2026-09-12 de-DE navigation-free census, aligned against the en-US walk of the same day (#876) — and all five sit on census surface `arrange.window`, which no record covers, so `locale-propose.py --apply` will not cite one. The citation gap is in the pipeline, not in the reading: `apply` keys records by the census row's RAW surface field, and every window row carries `arrange.window` whatever it is classified as. Fixing that is a change to the campaign for every locale at once and is deliberately not made while adding one."
